# Validate Input
'''
It is a good practice to validate any input from the user. In the
example above, an error will occur if the user inputs something
other than a number.

To avoid getting an error, we can test the input, and if it is 
not a number, the user could get a message like 'Wrong input, 
please try again', and allowed to make a new input:
'''
y = True
while y == True:
  x = input("Enter a number:")
  try:
    x = float(x);
    y = False
  except:
    print("Wrong input, please try again.")

